# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, *correct*.
#
# The two entries that matter for correctness rather than speed are
# `frontend/dist` and `var/`. A developer's `dist` would otherwise be copied
# into the context and could be layered over the one the Node stage builds,
# which is exactly the "stale artefact ships" failure the SERVE_SPA boot check
# exists to catch -- and it would pass, because a stale index.html is still an
# index.html. `var/` holds local databases and blobs, which have no business
# in an image at all.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local state: databases, blobs, e2e fixtures. Never in an image.
var/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Built and installed artefacts -- the Node stage builds dist/ itself.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Python caches and tooling state
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets and local configuration. `.env` must never be baked into a layer;
# the deployment supplies configuration at run time (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Repository furniture the runtime never reads
docs/
design-system/
eval/
tests/
.superpowers/
.kiro/
.claude/
*.md
!README.md
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
